<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended May 23, compared with the May 16 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.52 vs 5.49</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.10 vs 5.05</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.70 vs 5.69</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.63 vs 5.63</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.71 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.70 vs 5.68</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.96 vs 6.90</p>
</text>
